> He [[Peter]] persuaded, at the same time, those that were with him, and
pointed out that, unless the Holy Ghost had rested upon them, there might have
been some one who would have raised objections to their baptism. And the
apostles who were with James allowed the Gentiles to act freely, yielding us
up to the Spirit of God. But they themselves, while knowing the same God,
continued in the ancient observances; so that even Peter, fearing also lest
